fact WorkItem(id: "WI-661", description: some(value: "UMBRELLA / TRACKING (from a 2026-07-08 rules_by_functor <-> carrier-agnostic-heads design session, following the WI-656/659/655 index perf work). GOAL: retire the remaining term/TermId assumptions that keep the KB from FULLY carrier-agnostic (Value::Node/Entity) rule heads + stored terms, so hash-consing stays a pure OPTIMIZATION (CLAUDE.md Representation note) not a hard requirement. CRUX findings that make this tractable: (1) the CORE resolver (resolve.rs) does NOT use rules_by_functor -- goal-matching is discrimination-tree-based (gamma_candidates_for), already carrier-agnostic (view-driven discrim insert_pattern handles Node value heads, WI-348). So rules_by_functor is purely AUXILIARY. (2) Both rule indexes are ALREADY carrier-agnostic at INSERT: rules_by_functor keys on Symbol via TermView::head().functor_sym() (mod.rs:1076), discrim via the view-driven insert. (3) The rule_head term-only-reader PANIC ('a value fact reached a term-only head reader', a WI-348 trip-wire) is NOT an architectural barrier -- it can be lowered to a graceful LoadError (loud-but-not-fatal, per the repo 'loud error over silent skip' principle), making a value head in an un-migrated reader a MIGRATION DIAGNOSTIC, not a crash. THREE BUCKETS: (1) by-subfield SCANS over rules_by_functor -> replace with typed by-key indexes. DONE: WI-656 (op_records / OperationInfo), WI-659 (SortAliasIndex). OPEN: WI-660 (SortProvidesInfo); TODO: SortInfo, RequiresInfo. Removes most term-only rule_head/fact_head_term reads from hot paths. Tail: rules_by_functor's per-call fresh-Vec<RuleId> alloc (~50 sites) -> an impl-Iterator variant for the LEGITIMATE enumerators that survive (rule_ids_by_qn for `using X` fan-out, reflection, the index builders). (2) term-only STORAGE holdouts (a carrier-bearing thing pinned to a hash-consed TermId): rule_head reads -> migrate to rule_head_value/TermView, panic -> LoadError (child WI); and RequiresEntry.spec:TermId -> Value (child WI) -- sort-level requires, still term-only although op-level OpInfoRecord.requires already = Vec<Value> via WI-366 B2 (the asymmetry). Templates: WI-394 (remove term-only walk_type -> carrier-agnostic walk_view), WI-366 B2, WI-482. (3) TermId-as-KEY on NOMINAL sort identities (by_sort/by_domain/sort_info/entity_parent = HashMap<TermId,...>) -> LEAVE AS-IS: legitimate hash-consing per the CLAUDE.md note (nominal sort identities); its one fragility is canonicalization (the WI-581 same-FQN-copy assert). NOT a single deliverable -- a DIRECTION; land the concrete children incrementally, each green + /code-review, no big-bang. Children: RequiresEntry.spec->Value; rule_head->LoadError+TermView reader migration; (bucket-1) WI-660 + SortInfo/RequiresInfo indexes + rules_by_functor iterator variant."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-07-11T06:07:42Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-661", name: "carrier-agnostic")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-661", author: "user", content: "WI-660 impl (2026-07-09) confirms the concrete lever. WI-660's by_carrier index must key by SHORT-NAME (last segment) + a same_symbol re-filter, NOT canonical_sym like by_spec_base, because the carrier-direction provider sites compare with same_symbol (typing.rs) -- non-canonical and NON-transitive (a bare 'Main' bridges BOTH anthill.cli.Main and anthill.todo.Main, which do not bridge each other). The PRODUCER already resolves carriers (maybe_emit_fact_provides_info builds sort_ref from the resolved enclosing domain; a probe found 0/74 bare carriers in stdlib+repo load), so the residual reason same_symbol is needed is bare/unresolved carrier QUERY symbols reaching the consumers from the typer's dispatch. LEVER: canonicalize the carrier QUERY symbols at their dispatch producers (the call sites passing recv_sort/carrier_sym) so same_symbol collapses to canonical_sym everywhere -> the carrier consumers switch same_symbol->canonical_sort_sym, and WI-660's by_carrier can drop the short-name key + re-filter and key by canonical_sym like by_spec_base. Until then, short-name + same_symbol re-filter is the faithful, self-contained key.", at: "2026-07-08T21:46:40Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-661", author: "user", content: "PROGRESS 2026-07-10: bucket-1 SortInfo index DELIVERED as WI-673 (SortInfoIndex, short-name bucket + per-site re-filter, mirrors WI-660 ProvidesIndex.by_carrier). Migrated the 4 per-query keyed SortInfo lookups (find_sort_info the O(sorts^2) one, operations_of_sort, collect_sort_operations, sort_operation_names); LEFT the 4 enumerate-all SortInfo builders (build_base_substitutions, register_induction_axiom_witnesses, sorts_and_own_ops, sorts_with_constructors) as direct scans -- they need ALL facts, belong to the iterator-variant tail. Simpler lifecycle than provides: SortInfo frozen after the file-load loop (emit_sort_info only producer, emits Term::Ref name), so reset-at-load-phase-start + build-at-type_check-start, NO eq_derive rebuild pair, NO constant guard. BUCKET STATUS NOW: bucket-1 DONE = WI-656 (op_records), WI-659 (SortAlias), WI-660 (SortProvides), WI-673 (SortInfo). bucket-1 REMAINING = (a) SortRequiresInfo scan -- DEFERRED as low-value: only 1 keyed site (direct_requires, already memoized in requires_tree_cache), the other 2 sites are an enumerate-all mutator (resolve_requires_bindings) + witness pass; NOTE SortRequiresInfo is MUTATED during load (resolve_requires_bindings retract+reassert) so any index MUST build strictly after resolve_instantiations (type_check start satisfies it). (b) the rules_by_functor per-call fresh-Vec<RuleId> alloc -> impl-Iterator variant for the ~surviving legitimate enumerators (using-X fan-out, reflection, the index builders, the enumerate-all passes). bucket-2 (WI-662 RequiresEntry.spec, WI-663 rule_head readers) fully DONE. bucket-3 LEAVE AS-IS.", at: "2026-07-10T04:39:31Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-661", author: "user", content: "PROGRESS 2026-07-11: bucket-1 index CONSOLIDATION delivered as WI-676. The 3rd/4th hand-rolled per-fact index copies (ProvidesIndex WI-660, SortInfoIndex WI-673) now share ONE SymbolKeyedFactIndex (HashMap<Symbol,Vec<RuleId>> bucket; canonical-key get(); rids_or_scan fast-path-or-scan helper). ProvidesIndex = two of them (by_spec_base + by_carrier); SortInfoIndex struct DELETED (sort_info_index is now Option<SymbolKeyedFactIndex>). Folded the 3 near-dup accessors + 3 X_rids_by_Y wrappers into the shared struct. op_records + SortAliasIndex deliberately NOT folded (not Symbol->Vec<RuleId> buckets). Pure behavior-preserving refactor, full suite 2686/0; /code-review high (2 agents, correctness+removed-behavior+cross-file+cleanup/altitude/conventions): 0 correctness/dangle findings, 1 visibility nit (get pub(crate)->private) APPLIED. UMBRELLA STATUS: buckets 2 (WI-662/663) + 3 (leave-as-is) DONE; bucket-1 index migrations + consolidation DONE (WI-656/659/660/673 + WI-676). Bucket-1 REMAINING is only low-value polish: (a) SortRequiresInfo scan [deferred: 1 keyed site, already memoized]; (b) rules_by_functor per-call Vec->impl-Iterator tail [low-value: the benefiting alloc sites are annotated cold/rare by their authors, perf sub-noise per WI-673]. Substantive carrier-agnostic work is COMPLETE; what remains is optional cleanup.", at: "2026-07-11T05:19:26Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-661", author: "user", content: "PROGRESS 2026-07-11 (2): bucket-1 (b) reduce-sites delivered as WI-677. Added borrowing rules_by_functor_iter (same non-retracted filter + order as owned); migrated the 9 read-only sites that allocated a Vec just to reduce it (is_empty x3, any x4, first x1, find x1) -> early-exit + no alloc. Pure behavior-preserving; suite 2686/0; /code-review high (2 agents) 0 findings (incl. a proven laziness-safety check: no interior mutability on the filter inputs). SCOPE was the genuine-win reduce-sites ONLY -- the remaining (b) work (kb-mutating for-loops = borrow-conflict; enumerate-all for-loops = no early-exit, only alloc) is LEFT as documented low-value churn. UMBRELLA STATE: substantive carrier-agnostic work COMPLETE (buckets 2/3, bucket-1 index migrations + consolidation WI-676, bucket-1 (b) reduce-sites WI-677). Only genuinely-remaining items = (a) SortRequiresInfo typed index [deferred: 1 keyed site already memoized] + (b) full for-loop sweep [low-value churn, explicitly out of scope]. WI-661 can be CLOSED whenever the user wants -- nothing high-value left.", at: "2026-07-11T05:48:19Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-661", author: "user", content: "CLOSING 2026-07-11 (substantively complete). All buckets landed: bucket 2 = WI-662 (RequiresEntry.spec TermId->Value) + WI-663 (carrier-agnostic head readers); bucket 3 (TermId-as-key on nominal sort identities) = leave-as-is by design; bucket 1 = index migrations WI-656/659/660/673 + consolidation WI-676 (SymbolKeyedFactIndex) + WI-677 (rules_by_functor_iter reduce-sites). The rule_head panic the umbrella first wanted lowered to LoadError was instead resolved BETTER by WI-663 (keep-panic-where-a-skip-would-be-unsound + migrate readers). GOAL ACHIEVED: hash-consing is now an optimization, not a hard requirement, for the heads/storage the umbrella targeted; the core resolver was already discrim-tree/view-driven (carrier-agnostic). DEFERRED as LOW-VALUE (NOT tracked here -- re-file a fresh ticket if ever wanted): (a) a SortRequiresInfo keyed-lookup INDEX -- SortRequiresInfo is a RELATION scanned by direct_requires, whose 1 per-query site is already memoized in requires_tree_cache; an index would also have to build after resolve_instantiations since resolve_requires_bindings mutates the relation; (b) the FULL rules_by_functor->impl-Iterator sweep over the kb-MUTATING for-loops (shared borrow conflicts) + enumerate-all for-loops (no early-exit) -- only the Vec alloc would be saved, which authors annotated cold/rare and WI-673 measured sub-noise. Closing as Delivered.", at: "2026-07-11T06:07:40Z")
